WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.360
Here's a pretty flower that knits
quickly without hand manipulation.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.800
It's worked in multiples of 10,
but you can vary the multiple and change

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.040
the finished size of the flower
by changing the number of stitches.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.440
I cast on 100 stitches
with waste yarn and ravel cord.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.800
This gives you somewhere to hang the cast
on comb and weights,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.600
making knitting easier.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.854
The cast on edge will be the edges
of the flower, so use contrasting

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.920
yarn or a decorative cast on.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.000
For this flower, I just e wrapped
with two strands of the dark color.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.320
For this flower, I used a picot cast on.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.560
Once your cast on is complete,
put all the needles into hold position

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.640
and set your carriage to hold.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.720
Put 10 needles next to the carriage
into working position.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.920
Thread up your main color
Yarn and knit two rows.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.160
There's no need to wrap anything.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.800
Now put 10 more needles into working
position and knit another two rows.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.560
Continue knitting this way,
adding needles into work every other row.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.480
Can you see the long skinny
triangle taking shape?

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.360
When you finish the last section,
make sure your carriage is on the right.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.600
Break the yarn, leaving a tail.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.120
Using a double eyed needle,
remove all the stitches to the tail.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:32.000
I like to keep the waste yarn
on temporarily and block the piece.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:41.120
Now pull up the tail of yarn and gather
up the piece forming the flower shape.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.440
Secure the ends with
the tails of the yarn.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.694
You can stitch the flower directly
to a garment or attach it

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.200
to a pin for easy removal.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.160
These little accessories can add just
the right touch to your knitting.

